{
  "title": "Praise to the Lord, the Almighty",
  "author": "Joachim Neander (1650-1680); tr. Catherine Winkworth (1827-1878)",
  "key": "F",
  "public_domain": true,
  "arrangement": [
    "Verse 1",
    "Verse 2",
    "Verse 3",
    "Verse 4"
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "label": "Verse 1",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "1",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Praise to the Lord, the Almighty, the King of creation!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 26,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 38,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 49,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "O my soul, praise Him, for He is thy health and salvation!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 11,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 27,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 37,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 51,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "All ye who hear, now to His temple draw near;",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 11,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 28,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Praise Him in glad adoration!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 2",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "2",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Praise to the Lord, who o’er all things so wondrously reigneth,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 29,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 43,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 54,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shelters thee under His wings, yea, so gently sustaineth!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 24,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 39,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 49,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hast thou not seen how thy desires e’er have been",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 29,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Granted in what He ordaineth?",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 11,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 21,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 3",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "3",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Praise to the Lord, who doth prosper thy work and defend thee!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 29,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 41,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 52,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Surely His goodness and mercy here daily attend thee.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 11,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 24,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 35,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 43,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ponder anew what the Almighty can do,",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 8,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 23,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If with His love He befriend thee.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 12,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 22,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "label": "Verse 4",
      "kind": "verse",
      "color_hex": "#2378C3",
      "hotkey": "4",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Praise to the Lord! O let all that is in me adore Him!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 26,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 38,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 45,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "All that hath life and breath, come now with praises before Him!",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 14,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 31,
              "text": "Dm"
            },
            {
              "position": 45,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 55,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Let the Amen sound from His people again:",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 9,
              "text": "F"
            },
            {
              "position": 28,
              "text": "C"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Gladly for aye we adore Him.",
          "chords": [
            {
              "position": 0,
              "text": "Bb"
            },
            {
              "position": 11,
              "text": "C"
            },
            {
              "position": 19,
              "text": "F"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
